(6212918, 917091, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like this image a lot, I feel placed at the scene, part of it - and a little furtive as a result. The tones combined with the glowing highlights give it an otherworldly feel; rather reminiscent of a ''B'' science fiction movie. I get the sense an alien body snatcher is about to walk into the scene at any moment! Movie feeling aside, the architecture is interesting - those distant windows hold the eye very well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nicely made indeed.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like this image a lot, I feel placed at the scene, part of it - and a little furtive as a result. The tones combined with the glowing highlights give it an otherworldly feel; rather reminiscent of a ''B'' science fiction movie. I get the sense an alien body snatcher is about to walk into the scene at any moment! Movie feeling aside, the architecture is interesting - those distant windows hold the eye very well. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Very nicely made indeed.', '2010-11-05 12:51:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212928, 915715, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The combination of still elements and dynamic blurriness is fascinating; you''ve managed to communicate more of the scene as a result; we are transported here, not consigned to remain apart as mere viewer. The coloration is beautiful - the blue to transitions are quite lovely.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I wonder about the foreground reddish brown tones - they perhaps are a little strong and draw the eye from the more comfortable areas of the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: I agree... the stuff of dreams.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The combination of still elements and dynamic blurriness is fascinating; you''ve managed to communicate more of the scene as a result; we are transported here, not consigned to remain apart as mere viewer. The coloration is beautiful - the blue to transitions are quite lovely. Critical stuff: I wonder about the foreground reddish brown tones - they perhaps are a little strong and draw the eye from the more comfortable areas of the image. Overall: I agree... the stuff of dreams.', '2010-11-05 13:01:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212947, 916033, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I took quite a lot of time just looking at this one. Super-bold; I like that. I''m intrigued by the surface.... a reflection in metal? I see a silhouette but I don''t know its relationship to.... well, to the world really. Where does the light come from? Is that hair? Is that an arm? What is the source of the coloration? Did you intend for the marks and scratches to create the shape of rudimentary features? Endless fascinations.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing.<br/> <br/>Overall: In a DPC Free Study there are Apples and there are Pears, this is definitely a Pomegranate (and a Pointy one at that.)</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I took quite a lot of time just looking at this one. Super-bold; I like that. I''m intrigued by the surface.... a reflection in metal? I see a silhouette but I don''t know its relationship to.... well, to the world really. Where does the light come from? Is that hair? Is that an arm? What is the source of the coloration? Did you intend for the marks and scratches to create the shape of rudimentary features? Endless fascinations. Critical stuff: Nothing. Overall: In a DPC Free Study there are Apples and there are Pears, this is definitely a Pomegranate (and a Pointy one at that.)', '2010-11-05 13:18:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212953, 916842, 100393, '<td valign="top">Transcends the ''simple'' macro - this is something beautiful to boot. Front page stuff.</td>', 'Transcends the ''simple'' macro - this is something beautiful to boot. Front page stuff.', '2010-11-05 13:19:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212959, 914323, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wonderful framing! Lovely portrait image with bags of background interest making for a very strong story. For my money, a perfect conversion too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m surprised I haven''t seen it on 1x.com - I''m confident it would get published there.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wonderful framing! Lovely portrait image with bags of background interest making for a very strong story. For my money, a perfect conversion too. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: I''m surprised I haven''t seen it on 1x.com - I''m confident it would get published there.', '2010-11-05 13:21:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212961, 916112, 459, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  Love the detail and the "pose".</td>', 'Beautiful.  Love the detail and the "pose".', '2010-11-05 13:22:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212972, 917495, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: As soon as this came up on my screen it communicated ''cleavage'' - probably says more about me than your image. Once that image stuck though the small circular elements became some transparent gossamer... Certainly the shapes here hold interest and I commend your for in something so unconventional.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: This feels very minimal - in that it has minimal information with which we can build a picture. The near grey coloration does little to help out. I think perhaps a coloration other than grey may have worked a little better.<br/> <br/>Overall: Interesting but not very accessible - like a private joke that we are not part of, I think the viewer is excluded a little here. I''m not sure that''s ever a good thing.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: As soon as this came up on my screen it communicated ''cleavage'' - probably says more about me than your image. Once that image stuck though the small circular elements became some transparent gossamer... Certainly the shapes here hold interest and I commend your for in something so unconventional. Critical stuff: This feels very minimal - in that it has minimal information with which we can build a picture. The near grey coloration does little to help out. I think perhaps a coloration other than grey may have worked a little better. Overall: Interesting but not very accessible - like a private joke that we are not part of, I think the viewer is excluded a little here. I''m not sure that''s ever a good thing.', '2010-11-05 13:28:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212975, 916047, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I was always going to be drawn to this one - great POV, wonderful lighting, lovely tones, excellent textures, eclectic composition, fabulous shadow. What more could we want?<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like this.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I was always going to be drawn to this one - great POV, wonderful lighting, lovely tones, excellent textures, eclectic composition, fabulous shadow. What more could we want? Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: I really like this.', '2010-11-05 13:31:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6212978, 916437, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This works really well. The even illumination and superb clarity elevates this image above a shot of a street scene - you''ve created something that didn''t necessarily come across in the real scene. You''ve have found and distilled the sign elements and have brought them all together, like a single image montage (oxymoronic though that may be). I like how you''ve kept above the people space - inviting us to ''look up'' and see what you created above our heads.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Pretty inspired and bold to boot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This works really well. The even illumination and superb clarity elevates this image above a shot of a street scene - you''ve created something that didn''t necessarily come across in the real scene. You''ve have found and distilled the sign elements and have brought them all together, like a single image montage (oxymoronic though that may be). I like how you''ve kept above the people space - inviting us to ''look up'' and see what you created above our heads. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Pretty inspired and bold to boot.', '2010-11-05 13:32:26.000000', NULL, 1),
