(6215087, 916599, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great story here - I particularly like the suggestion of a second figure to the left of the door. I''m pretty convinced this would work nearly so well in colour - I think you''ve made a great choice going with monochrome.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: nothing much.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting image benefit from just enough ambiguity.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great story here - I particularly like the suggestion of a second figure to the left of the door. I''m pretty convinced this would work nearly so well in colour - I think you''ve made a great choice going with monochrome. Critical stuff: nothing much. Overall: An interesting image benefit from just enough ambiguity.', '2010-11-07 17:27:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215093, 914580, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great sense of scale here and your blue monochrome treatment works really well. The figure adds load of interest, without him the image would (I think) fail.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think a less tight crop on the bottom would''ve been better.<br/> <br/>Overall: More than the sum of its parts. I like that.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great sense of scale here and your blue monochrome treatment works really well. The figure adds load of interest, without him the image would (I think) fail. Critical stuff: I think a less tight crop on the bottom would''ve been better. Overall: More than the sum of its parts. I like that.', '2010-11-07 17:30:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215098, 915712, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the idea behind this shot - the semi-silhouettes, the overt grain and vignette, and the stark light. I wonder what their story is too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Your editing choices may be seen by some to be a little odd.<br/> <br/>Overall: An image that benefits from the understanding that less is sometimes / often more.<br/> <br/>[Not sure why my comment got truncated - finished it off now]<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-11-09 04:00:22.</i></td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the idea behind this shot - the semi-silhouettes, the overt grain and vignette, and the stark light. I wonder what their story is too. Critical stuff: Your editing choices may be seen by some to be a little odd. Overall: An image that benefits from the understanding that less is sometimes / often more. [Not sure why my comment got truncated - finished it off now]', '2010-11-07 17:35:05.000000', '2010-11-09 04:00:22.000000', 1),
(6215105, 916623, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Interesting image, interesting title. The purple area looks like it is something that has been embedded with a block of green glass. I like how it looks transparent.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: One of those where the image interest tops out pretty quickly.<br/> <br/>Overall: I quite like this image but I suspect many others aren''t not convinced.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Interesting image, interesting title. The purple area looks like it is something that has been embedded with a block of green glass. I like how it looks transparent. Critical stuff: One of those where the image interest tops out pretty quickly. Overall: I quite like this image but I suspect many others aren''t not convinced.', '2010-11-07 17:40:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215109, 917497, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Lovely geometry and colours - I''m a particular fan of the central red and green section. I also like the way the image confounds our sense of scale until we spot the bricks (which give us a good clue).<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m torn about the way the image is very flat - I''m sure that was your intention, but I''m not so sure it works.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Lovely geometry and colours - I''m a particular fan of the central red and green section. I also like the way the image confounds our sense of scale until we spot the bricks (which give us a good clue). Critical stuff: I''m torn about the way the image is very flat - I''m sure that was your intention, but I''m not so sure it works.', '2010-11-07 17:45:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215126, 917243, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the POV and the contrast of the road in this image. The fog bank / cloud adds a lot of interest too. I really like how quickly convergent the lines are, gives the image great perspective.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think I may have been tempted to manipulate the curve a little to tak the fog close to white.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like this short - lots of atmosphere.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the POV and the contrast of the road in this image. The fog bank / cloud adds a lot of interest too. I really like how quickly convergent the lines are, gives the image great perspective. Critical stuff: I think I may have been tempted to manipulate the curve a little to tak the fog close to white. Overall: I like this short - lots of atmosphere.', '2010-11-07 18:03:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215128, 916103, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wow - I''ve tried this many times and never got close to this level of quality. Well made indeed!</td>', 'Wow - I''ve tried this many times and never got close to this level of quality. Well made indeed!', '2010-11-07 18:04:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215131, 917182, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like how extreme and uncompromising this image island how you''ve reduced all the figures to just their forms (who needs texture!). I like where you''ve placed the horizon in the frame too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: I think the processing works really well for this scene.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like how extreme and uncompromising this image island how you''ve reduced all the figures to just their forms (who needs texture!). I like where you''ve placed the horizon in the frame too. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: I think the processing works really well for this scene.', '2010-11-07 18:07:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215135, 916886, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Just amazing! Superb clarity, wonderful texture, great light. Excellent use of negative space too. The blues and subtle orange / pink add some very special accents of colour to this image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great stuff.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Just amazing! Superb clarity, wonderful texture, great light. Excellent use of negative space too. The blues and subtle orange / pink add some very special accents of colour to this image. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Great stuff.', '2010-11-07 18:09:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215143, 917170, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Lovely scene, well captured. I like how everybody is just going about their business - that contributes greatly to the story-telling qualities of the image. The coloration is very nice indeed - it combines with the light to offer up a very relaxed mood.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not wholly convinced by the overall composition of the various elements.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like it well enough though.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Lovely scene, well captured. I like how everybody is just going about their business - that contributes greatly to the story-telling qualities of the image. The coloration is very nice indeed - it combines with the light to offer up a very relaxed mood. Critical stuff: I''m not wholly convinced by the overall composition of the various elements. Overall: I like it well enough though.', '2010-11-07 18:14:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215145, 917049, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very well made.</td>', 'Very well made.', '2010-11-07 18:14:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6215151, 917464, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Quite an extreme image - like all of the affordances of digital photography have been discarded. I do like the vintage coloration, the grain and the vignette though.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The overall level of sharpness looks a little off.<br/> <br/>Overall: Bold stuff; but I think it has some correctable elements.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Quite an extreme image - like all of the affordances of digital photography have been discarded. I do like the vintage coloration, the grain and the vignette though. Critical stuff: The overall level of sharpness looks a little off. Overall: Bold stuff; but I think it has some correctable elements.', '2010-11-07 18:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
