(6217105, 917467, 20168, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> Seriously, this is kinda getting a tad sad now.  You have done this so many times , it is stale. Kinda pathetic </i></td></tr></table> <br/>So not only are members regularly called out for not voting ''properly'' (trolls, etc), but are now called out for not taking the ''right'' kind of pictures as well?  I''m afraid that <i>that</i>, is pathetic.  Actually, it''s rather worse. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>When you see the same thing over and over again on purpose, just for the purpose of wanting the brown ribbon, it gets boring.  So , make me the bad person for knowing what a great tog Charlie is and knowing that he does this, cos he ''can''.  The first 10 times it was funny. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I appreciate that <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=87808" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">julietNN</a> found humor in at least 10 of these boring entries. I still have quite a long way to go before working my way around the RGB color wheel on my way to the true color of "brown". Tee Hee :)</td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: Originally posted by ubique: Originally posted by JulietNN: Seriously, this is kinda getting a tad sad now.  You have done this so many times , it is stale. Kinda pathetic  So not only are members regularly called out for not voting ''properly'' (trolls, etc), but are now called out for not taking the ''right'' kind of pictures as well?  I''m afraid that that, is pathetic.  Actually, it''s rather worse.   When you see the same thing over and over again on purpose, just for the purpose of wanting the brown ribbon, it gets boring.  So , make me the bad person for knowing what a great tog Charlie is and knowing that he does this, cos he ''can''.  The first 10 times it was funny.   I appreciate that  julietNN found humor in at least 10 of these boring entries. I still have quite a long way to go before working my way around the RGB color wheel on my way to the true color of "brown". Tee Hee :)', '2010-11-08 20:28:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6217123, 912812, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by louinsd:</b></div><hr/><i> pleasant colors... some detail would have been nice though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Any detail would have ruined it. I pressed 8.</td>', 'Originally posted by louinsd: pleasant colors... some detail would have been nice though.  Any detail would have ruined it. I pressed 8.', '2010-11-08 20:43:07.000000', NULL, 0),
